Carafe: FEX_GDBSYMBOLS can be passed to FEX, so a profiling run maps every x86 instruction to its ARM64 code.
FEX puts an x86 instruction into a block's RIP map only when it can fault, unless GDBSymbols is on
(Core.cpp:647-649). Register-only instructions such as fcom st(1), fnstsw ax and test ah are then charged to
the instruction before them. With FEX_GDBSYMBOLS=1 every instruction gets an entry; under mingw the GDB
interface itself is a stub (GDBJIT.cpp:116), and the emitted code is the same: checked on 26 blocks.
Off unless a program's settings turn it on.
LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the file it changes.

--- a/horizon-wine/source/fex_options.h
+++ b/horizon-wine/source/fex_options.h
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
     NX_FEX_X87_CONVERSION_ROUNDING,
     NX_FEX_X87_FAST_STACK,
     NX_FEX_X87_SINGLE_PRECISION,
+    NX_FEX_GDB_SYMBOLS,
     NX_FEX_OPTION_COUNT
 };
 
@@ -122,6 +123,9 @@
     { NX_FEX_X87_SINGLE_PRECISION, "FEX_X87SINGLEPRECISION",
       "With reduced x87 precision, computes x87 math in 32-bit floats, as Direct3D 9 games set the precision to.",
       1, 0, 2, { "0", "1" }, { "0 - Off", "1 - On" } },
+    { NX_FEX_GDB_SYMBOLS, "FEX_GDBSYMBOLS",
+      "Records every x86 instruction in each translated block's address map, so the profiler names each one. The code is the same.",
+      1, 0, 2, { "0", "1" }, { "0 - Off", "1 - On" } },
 };
 
 static inline int nx_fex_option_choice( const struct nx_fex_option *option, const char *value )
